956
01:32:34,430 --> 01:32:39,810
但同样，如果收到信号，我们也可以稍微提前布局。
But equally, we can be a little more preemptive if we get one of the signals as mentioned.

958
01:32:40,310 --> 01:32:43,188
杠杆。这是一个可以高杠杆操作的策略。
Leveraging. This is a strategy where you can get highly leveraged.

959
01:32:43,188 --> 01:32:46,589
因为回报非常好，止损非常紧。
Simply because you’ve got a really good reward. Very, very tight stop.

961
01:32:46,930 --> 01:32:50,574
最终，有获取高收益的潜力。
And ultimately, the potential for a very good gain. All right.

962
01:32:50,574 --> 01:32:54,549
在技巧方面，全世界都能看到突破。
In terms of the tip, The entire universe can see the breakout.

963
01:32:55,070 --> 01:32:57,830
好的。记住这一点。所有人都能看到突破机会。
Okay. Note that. Everyone can see a breakout opportunity.

964
01:32:58,970 --> 01:33:04,390
但成功的参与者对突破采用一致的方法。
However, successful participants employ a consistent approach to breakouts.

965
01:33:05,170 --> 01:33:07,210
学会它。别忘了。
Learn it. And don’t forget it.

966
01:33:07,570 --> 01:33:11,010
好，大家。现在进入下一个扩展阅读。
All right, guys. Let’s now move on to the next of our additional readings.

967
01:33:15,670 --> 01:33:18,770
这是Ryan Holiday推荐的第二本书。
This is the second recommended book from Ryan Holiday.

968
01:33:19,430 --> 01:33:21,910
第一本显然是《障碍即道路》。
Obviously, the first was *The Obstacle Is the Way*.

969
01:33:21,910 --> 01:33:25,030
第二本是《自负是敌人》。好书。非常好的书。
The second is *Ego Is the Enemy*. Great book. Fantastic book.

970
01:33:25,830 --> 01:33:28,930
真的能引发你很多思考。
It really provokes your thought quite a lot.

971
01:33:30,690 --> 01:33:34,350
书中总结：这是对‘自负’的‘如何’和‘为何’的深入研究。
Note a summary of it: It’s a researched understanding of the *how* and *why* of the ego.

973
01:33:34,470 --> 01:33:37,713
它让你深刻理解人们为何会产生自负，
So, it gives you a really good understanding of why people develop an ego,

974
01:33:37,713 --> 01:33:40,029
甚至那些原本没有自负的人为何突然有了自负，
what makes even people without an ego suddenly develop one,

975
01:33:40,029 --> 01:33:42,347
以及自负为何最终是坏事。
and ultimately, why the ego is such a bad thing.

976
01:33:43,050 --> 01:33:50,990
在行动层面，非常发人深省。
Now, in terms of action, very thought-provoking. It’s definitely going to give you a mindset shift.

978
01:33:51,070 --> 01:33:53,614
肯定会让你想改变对自负的看法，
It’s definitely going to make you want to adjust how you think about the ego,

979
01:33:53,614 --> 01:33:54,409
以及它最终的含义。
and what it ultimately means.

981
01:33:59,230 --> 01:34:03,270
不断质疑自己对自我的理解和自负。
Consistent questioning of your own understanding of the self and the ego.

983
01:34:03,270 --> 01:34:04,550
我认为这是关键收获。
I think this is the key takeaway.

984
01:34:04,710 --> 01:34:07,150
你会不断自问：我有自负吗？
You’re going to constantly be saying to yourself: Do I have an ego?

986
01:34:07,270 --> 01:34:09,610
它是否在我的理解中制造偏见？
Is it creating bias in my understanding?

987
01:34:10,150 --> 01:34:11,290
是否制造了障碍？
Is it creating a block?

988
01:34:11,490 --> 01:34:12,670
成长型思维的缺失？
A lack of growth mindset?

989
01:34:12,830 --> 01:34:15,930
诸如此类。永远保持学习者心态。
All these sorts of things. Always stay a student.

990
01:34:16,030 --> 01:34:17,010
这是其中一个关键亮点。
This is one of the key highlights.

991
01:34:17,530 --> 01:34:21,190
理解我们总能成长、学习，并追求更好的自己。
Understand we can always grow, learn, and strive for a better version of ourselves.

993
01:34:21,390 --> 01:34:22,610
这是其中一个关键亮点。
This is one of the key highlights.

994
01:34:23,110 --> 01:34:25,810
有了自负，我们就无法有效成长。
With an ego, we can’t grow as effectively.

995
01:34:25,810 --> 01:34:32,270
书中花了很多时间讲这一点。自负是自然现象。
And this is something the book spends a lot of time going over. Obviously, ego is a natural occurrence.

997
01:34:32,830 --> 01:34:37,050
但通过实用的解决方案，你可以驯服它，控制它，从而做出更好决策。
But with practical solutions, you can tame it and control it to make better decisions.

999
01:34:37,210 --> 01:34:41,830
所以，重点不是消除自负。我们都有。必须与之共存。
So, again, it’s not about eradicating the ego. We’ve all got it. We have to live with it.

1000
01:34:41,970 --> 01:34:47,250
而是理解它，以及它在我们内心中最终扮演的角色——
But it’s about understanding it, and what role it ultimately plays within us—

1001
01:34:47,250 --> 01:34:52,530
如何利用自负为我所用，而不是被其所害。
how we can utilize the ego to our advantage rather than to our disadvantage.

1003
01:34:53,130 --> 01:34:58,030
最后，衡量表现时，不是看结果，而是用记分卡。
And then, lastly, to measure performance, not on outcome, but with a scorecard.

1005
01:34:58,330 --> 01:34:59,110
这见解很深刻。
This is quite insightful.

1006
01:35:00,110 --> 01:35:02,770
是本书很棒的结尾部分。
A great final section to the book.

1007
01:35:02,790 --> 01:35:03,730
我强烈推荐这本书。
I highly recommend this book.

1008
01:35:04,110 --> 01:35:08,977
它的目的是激发你的思考，
Again, it is there to provoke your thought and ultimately give you a better understanding

1009
01:35:08,977 --> 01:35:12,547
最终让你更清楚自己的自我如何阻碍你。
of how your ego might ultimately be standing in the way.

1012
01:35:12,910 --> 01:35:14,170
好，我们来总结一下。
All right. Let's go wrap up then.

1013
01:35:14,430 --> 01:35:16,290
